    "updated_at": "2026-07-15T14:06:53Z",
    "body": "> I guess I could see us adding another boolean, but this one is rather murky. \n\nMaybe it can be something a bit more encompassing like `removeUnsafeValues` that effectively maps to safe vs. unsfae and cannot become false when calling the \"safe\" variants.\n \n> Do we have to address this now or could we conceivably add this later if it becomes a pain point?\n\nIt might bring some web compat issues later to make `removeUnsafe` more strict in the future. But probably not huge ones.",
